cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this archive, please cite it and the article it accompanies."
type: software
title: "KeepCount: conditions, code, records and history"
abstract: >-
  The conditions, code, records, notes and git history of an audit of what images of behavioral data keep, applied to
  a transform that turns keystroke times into shaded tiles, one per sentence, through speed and rest (runs v1 to
  v6j), and, from version 1.1.0, the conditions, code and tests of the same audit applied to the pause summaries that
  writing research reports (runs v6k to v6s), with the values that article writes and the record cells they come
  from; the records of v6k to v6s are not shared and are rebuilt from the public data. Every computation ran a script
  on conditions committed before the script was first run. The keystroke data are not redistributed. The code (src/, works/*.py, tools/, tests/, article/jowr/values/*.py) is under the MIT License (LICENSE); the documents,
  conditions, records, texts and images are under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (LICENSE-docs).
